# Vercel Speed Insights Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the Arozao e-commerce platform (Next.js 14.2.25 with App Router).

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Added dependency**: `@vercel/speed-insights` version ^2.1.0
- **Package manager**: npm (npm 10.9.9)
- **Lock file created**: package-lock.json

### 2. Code Changes

#### Modified: `app/layout.tsx`
- Added import statement for SpeedInsights component from `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
- Integrated `<SpeedInsights />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag, after all other providers and components
- Placement ensures optimal performance tracking while maintaining existing app structure

### 3. Implementation Details
Following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), the implementation:
- Uses the Next.js-specific integration path (`@vercel/speed-insights/next`)
- Places the component in the root layout to track all pages
- Maintains the existing provider hierarchy and component structure
- Preserves all existing functionality and styling

### 4. Verification
- ✅ TypeScript type checking passed (`npm run typecheck`)
- ✅ Production build completed successfully (`npm run build`)
- ✅ All 387 pages generated without errors
- ✅ No breaking changes to existing functionality

## Files Modified
- `arozao/app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights component
- `arozao/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency

## Files Created
- `arozao/package-lock.json` - Dependency lock file for npm

## Next Steps
Once deployed to Vercel:
1. Speed Insights will automatically start collecting performance metrics
2. Data will be accessible from the Vercel dashboard under Speed Insights
3. The tracking script will be served from `/_vercel/speed-insights/*` routes
4. Real User Monitoring (RUM) data will be collected from actual user visits

## Notes
- The SpeedInsights component is lightweight and won't impact page load performance
- All metrics are collected anonymously and securely
- No additional configuration is required - it works out of the box on Vercel deployments
